WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.500
first FDA submission for the therapeutic use of an antibody oligoconjugate. That FDA submission

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:15.480
is for accelerated approval in the DMD44, Saxon 44, skipping using dystrophin as a surrogate

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:21.140
biomarker. We previously received FDA breakthrough therapy designation for this. The submission

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:27.080
package is based on the outstanding data that we had in the Explore 44 study as well as long-term

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:33.160
follow-up. And we expect the first launch here in the first half of 27 with the ongoing phase

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:39.240
studies ongoing. We have multiple follow-on programs now targeting additional exons that

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:44.220
we'll be bringing forward as well. So we're quite excited to leverage this technology to take on

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.460
DMD across multiple areas.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:52.340
And then with respect to the Delbrax data, we read out in the quarter as well that the phase 1-2

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:59.860
study at the target dose that we are taking into phase 3 studies met its primary and key secondary

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:07.740
biomarker endpoints. So as a reminder, this is a study that looked at KHDC1L and creatine

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:15.460
kinase reductions in the plasma. KHDC1L is a protein that's downstream. It's a protein that's

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:24.020
believed to be regulated by Dux4, Dux4 being the gene that's impacted in FSHD. And so having

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:29.080
these plasma biomarkers indicates that we have strong target engagement and muscle damage

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:33.800
reduction as indicated by the statistically significant creatine kinase reductions that we

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:39.940
saw. Our base case remains a submission in 2028. But based on the data that we've seen in the

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:45.460
biomarkers and ongoing work we're currently conducting to hopefully correlate the

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:53.820
biomarkers to Dux4 as well as clinical improvements in these patients. We plan to engage FDA and other

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:59.960
regulatory authorities in the coming months. And then we'll ultimately provide an update if those

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:05.000
regulatory authorities support our ability to file this medicine based on this data.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:11.960
Now moving to slide 16. So we're on track for a busy second half. We already had four readouts in the

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:15.480
first half. In the second half, we expect we'll see some improvement. We're going to see some

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:22.440
improvement with pellicarsin, remibrutinib, and daldiserin readouts in the coming months. And then before the end of the year,

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:31.240
readouts for yonalimab, Revcedo, and HS, as well as additional readouts for phase two programs, QCZ484,

